    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d290">

                <pb facs="0748" n="662" xml:id="pg662"/>

                <head>No. 287.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. <persName type="from"
                            >Nelson</persName> to Mr. <persName corresp="#p_HF1" type="to"
                            >Fish</persName>.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United
                                States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1873-03-31"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 31, 1873</date>. (Received April
                        15.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 721.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The federal troops under the command of
                    Generals Corona and Ceballos reached the capital of the district of Tepic
                    without any resistance after capturing the principal towns. Lozada, the chief of
                    the rebels, has been abandoned by his troops, who submitted to the supreme
                    government, offering their services and arms against their former commander. The
                    revolt may, therefore, be considered as substantially ended.</p>
                <p>The national Congress commences its regular sessions on the 1st of April,
                    (to-morrow.) At a preliminary meeting of the deputies a few days ago, Mr.
                    Francisco Gomez Palacio was elected president of Congress for the month of
                    April, and Mr. Julio Zarat vice-president. The former gentleman is supposed to
                    be opposed to the administration of President Lerdo. The national budget, the
                    accounts of the last fiscal year, and the proposed railway projects, will form
                    the principal subjects of discussion during the approaching session.</p>
                <p>Messrs. R. C. Ritter &amp; Co., American citizens, residing in Vera Cruz, and
                    agents of the Alexandre line of steamers, have made a contract with the Mexican
                    government to run a line of steamers between New Orleans and Vera Cruz for the
                    term of four years from November next, making semi-monthly voyages, going and
                    coming by way of Tuxpan and Tampico. The Mexican government is to pay them a
                    subvention of three thousand six hundred dollars per month.</p>
                <p>The <hi rendition="#italic">epizooty</hi> has appeared in almost every part of
                    the republic, attacking, at the same time, horses, mules, cattle, sheep, and
                    fowls. It has rarely proved fatal, and its epidemic character is rapidly
                    disappearing.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><persName>THOMAS H. NELSON</persName>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
